! ==============================================================================
! SPINLOOP -- minimal purpose-built story for bounded-termination testing
! (G1-A negative tests, Issue #11).  NOT part of the F01-F12 fixture.
! ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Original content authored for this project; same redistribution grant as the
! main fixture (see ../README.md): copy, modify, and redistribute freely.
!
! Main prints a start marker and then spins in a NONRECURSIVE infinite loop:
! no stack growth, no input boundary, no timer -- the Z-machine itself never
! yields.  A host-side deadline (killable worker thread or child watchdog) is
! therefore the only mechanism that can bound this story, which is exactly the
! property under test.  The Serial pin keeps recompilation byte-identical.
! ==============================================================================

Serial "261022";

[ Main;
    print "SPINLOOP-START^";
    while (1) { }
];
